> sometimes already after ca. 20 x 6.0 arrays (though my series are
> frequently > 100). I am hoping that the memory management under 64 bit
> may help here (the processes themselves are not that big; the max I
> have seen went into 2.5GB).

Just so we are one the same page, deleting .Rcache/ directory does not
make R consume more memory, but rather less.  Maybe that is what you
said, and by deleting those cache files you're saying then you're run
into memory problems.

There are some data structures that are stored locally (memory cache)
and it might be that they some how adds up, but they shouldn't.
There are ways to clean these out, but one has to know the object
where they are stored, e.g. the AffymetrixCdfFile object.

Next time, it would be great if you could provide a traceback on the
memory error message and the exact script up until and including the
step where you run out of memory.

/Henrik

