Subject: aroma.affymetrix v1.2.0 released
Message-ID: <eNjfGhTXN0o.IqLkBkKdYj4J@aroma-affymetrix.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/aroma-affymetrix/c/eNjfGhTXN0o/m/IqLkBkKdYj4J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

aroma.affymetrix v1.1.0 is available.  Please install/update by:

  source("http://www.braju.com/R/hbLite.R");
  hbInstall("aroma.affymetrix");

Although the above installation looks the same, under the hood more
and more packages are now installed from the CRAN repository.  It is
possible to install most of it directly from CRAN, but won't get
everything, which is the above is still the recommended solution.

An important update in this release is that static methods
fromChipType() and fromName() of AffymetrixCelSet and other classes
are now defunct (not working).  Instead, you have to use byChipType()
and byName() with everything else being the same.  On Windows it is
now possible to use Windows Shortcut links also in subdirectories,
e.g. rawData/MyDataSet/ -> somewhere else, and not only for linking
the root directory rawData/.  This improves the options where you can
put data files etc.  As usual there are a few bug fixes (thanks to
your reports) and the exception handling is getting better providing
more helpful error messages.  More details below.

Cheers,

Henrik Bengtsson & others

